<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gallo-Romans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gallo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> were the Romanised inhabitants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> from the Roman conquest to the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and following <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> and, by the 5th century, mostly Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, they formed the majority under the Visigothic, Burgundian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Frankish kingdoms</a>, whose kings kept separate laws for them. Their speech developed into French and Occitan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gallo-romans.jpg" alt="Gallo-Romans" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vassil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fresque_gallo-romaine_Evreux_210209.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
